{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794390233,"nonce":"2UkeEjUr0qCvbkRbltZbc1bTHck=","message":"Windows tests, first run with a working checkout (f49f77b1): 308 of 2664 fail, 306 of them at 'SDF Shadow Pipeline' creation. FXC (wgpu's DX12 compiler) rejects the generated fragment shader: X3533 non-empty case statements must have break or return, X3537 fall-through not allowed. Cause: the russl shadow match ends in a default arm of discard only; commit 7d60eae8 had put an explicit return inside that arm in the hand-written WGSL for exactly this, and the port dropped it. The HLSL DXC job passes because DXC does not reject it. Fix: return inside the arm, plus a test that converts every shader to HLSL (naga, shader model 5.1) and flags any switch case not ending in return/break/continue (fails on the three shadow shaders without the fix). The shadow pipeline failed first, so the 3D and notch pipelines were never reached by FXC on Windows: more FXC errors are possible and only Windows CI can show them.","files":null}]}